{"id":"word:hebrew:H1347","type":"word","title":"גָּאוֹן","subtitle":"H1347 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"the same as 1346","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גָּאוֹן (H1347) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 49 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גָּאוֹן (gâʼôwn) means the same as 1346 First listed occurrence: Amos 6 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גָּאוֹן","transliteration":"gâʼôwn","pronunciation":"gaw-ohn'","strong":"H1347","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1347","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["גְּא֣וֹן","גְּא֥וֹן","בִּ/גְא֣וֹן","לְ/גָא֣וֹן","גְאֽוֹן"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",23],["HR/Ncmsc",9],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",4],["HNcmsa",3],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",2],["HR/Ncmsa",2],["HC/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",2],["HNcmpc/Sp2fs",1],["HC/Ncmsa",1],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3mp",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"the same as 1346","usage":"arrogancy, excellency(-lent), majesty, pomp, pride, proud, swelling.","full":"H1347. ga 'own גָּאוֺן noun masculine Hosea 5:5 exaltation — Job 40:10 5 t.; construct גְּאוֺן Lev 26:19 31 t.; suffix גְּאוֺנְךָ etc. Exod 15:7 9 t.; plural suffix גְּאוֺנָ֑יִךְ Ezek 16:56 ; &#8212; 1 exaltation, majesty, excellence , a. of nations, their wealth, power, magnificence of buildings , e.g. Egypt Ezek 32:12 , Chaldeans Isa 13:11 , 19 ; 14:11 , Philistines Zech 9:6 , Assyria 10:11 , Jacob Psa 47:5 ; Amos 6:8 ; 8:7 ; Nahum 2:3 , Israel Hosea 5:5 ; 7:10 (probably appellation of ׳י ), Nahum 2:3 , Judah Jer 13:9 , Jerusalem 13:9 ; Ezek 16:56 ; עֻזָּהּ גְּאוֺן pride of her strength 30:6 , 18 ; 33:28 ; עזים גאון 7:24 (but ᵐ5 Ew Hi Co read עזם ); עזכם גאון Lev 26:19 ; Ezek 24:21 ; the fruit of land of Judah will become ולתפארת לגאון majestic and beautiful Isa 4:2 ; צבי כל גאון the majesty of all the splendour (of Tyre) 23:9 ; Zion is to become עולם גאון an everlasting excellency 60:15 . b. of God Exod 15:7 ; Isa 24:14 ; Micah 5:3 ; גְּאֹנוֺ הֲדַר Isa 2:10 , 19 , 21 ; גְּאוֺנוֺ בְּקוֺל יַרְעֵם Job 37:4 ; וָגֹבַהּ גָּאוֺן נָא עֲדֵה 40:10 . c. הירדן גאון majesty of Jordan , referring to the green and shady banks, clothed with willows, tamarisks, and cane, in which the lions made their covert Jer 49:19 ; 50:44 ; Zech 11:3 , and therefore dangerous Jer 12:5 (Ew thinks of the swelling of its agitated waters); גַּלֶּיךָ גְּאוֺן majesty of thy waves Job 38:11 . 2 pride (bad sense) Job 35:12 ; Psa 59:13 ; Prov 8:13 ; 16:18 ; Ezek 7:20 ; 16:49 ; Zeph 2:10 ; of Moab Isa 16:6 (twice in verse) = Jer 48:29 (twice in verse).","rootNote":"from 1342 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Amos 6 8","keyReferences":["Amos 6 8","Amos 8 7","Exod 15 7","Ezek 7 20","Ezek 7 24","Ezek 16 49","Ezek 16 56","Ezek 24 21"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":49,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Amos 6 8","book":"Amos","chapter":6,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּא֣וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"Amos 8 7","book":"Amos","chapter":8,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בִּ/גְא֣וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"Exod 15 7","book":"Exod","chapter":15,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּאוֹנְ/ךָ֖","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp2ms"},{"reference":"Ezek 7 20","book":"Ezek","chapter":7,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/גָא֣וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Ezek 7 24","book":"Ezek","chapter":7,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּא֣וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"Ezek 16 49","book":"Ezek","chapter":16,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גָּא֨וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Ezek 16 56","book":"Ezek","chapter":16,"verse":56,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּאוֹנָֽיִ/ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc/Sp2fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 24 21","book":"Ezek","chapter":24,"verse":21,"englishText":